  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Sometimes, the native eye tracking fails to synchronize to one or more remote players. To them, the avatar's eyes appear stuck looking straight ahead unblinking. The eye movements appear normal from the wearer's perspective.\n\nThis makes the native eye tracking basically useless given that I have to assume that at any given time it has just decided not to work for whoever I may be talking to. And there is no way to check from my end without asking every single other player \"are my eyes moving for you?\".\n\nUnfortunately I do not yet have a repro for this since it seems to happen intermittently. It is also difficult to even tell when it its happening because it requires the remote party to notice that it is happening and also decide to actually tell me.\n\n(If you ask anyone in the VRCFT discord they seem to be well acquainted with this issue, and yet I could not find a canny report for it. Apologies if this is a duplicate)",
